{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06FW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$x$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ec9e400664531bc6da5f5b56f36c1ebf0bbceff0956e36f95542d96426775668", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ab46853c19f6562c81caa0176ea17fd392ef49229b1ba732efc4ee37f5ddaa2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is another, more technical, characterization of a finite type\npoint on an algebraic stack. It tells us in particular that the residual\ngerbe of <MATH_0001> at <MATH_0002> exists whenever <MATH_0003> is a finite type point!\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c8621e0f92862de331129650c479499ea6240751d83ed89c5fa3e0846c239875", "unit_id": "tag:06FW:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06FW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$x$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{Z}|$", "MATH_0006": "$f : \\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{x\\} = |f|(|\\mathcal{Z}|)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$x$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-point-finite-type-monomorphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:532a2351f85fd44ebb4d03a3c1820bc7376bbaadd70ff57174c5b883e846a602", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:20fe8e95a5d75f7d2694ef53074814aaa3da84e84cab5419e817d340432a8735", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack.\nLet <MATH_0002>. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is a finite type point,\n<STRUCT_0003> there exists an algebraic stack <MATH_0004>\nwhose underlying topological space <MATH_0005> is a singleton,\nand a morphism <MATH_0006> which is\nlocally of finite type such that <MATH_0007>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> the residual gerbe <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009> at <MATH_0010> exists\nand the inclusion morphism <MATH_0011> is locally of\nfinite type.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b8e5d54a71dc158d3368299e464ec7a9de942dd0b51ad9960d652d282a054ca5", "unit_id": "tag:06G3:statement"}
